title: Your notes
pid: a428e50f-51cf-4782-b7c4-4848dc9c1564
body: |2-
  A high =•= ends the in-side of contains or of hides when a note of the
  user's graph -- a note homed in an owned skgrepo, which the skgrepo
  restriction shows ('docs/glossary.org', "integrated, the user's graph,
  kept elsewhere") -- is among its members. On contains it is one but
  the nearest node occurrence above the headline: the user keeps the
  node elsewhere too. On hides it is any. So =2a•C= says the viewparent
  and a note of yours contain it; =1•H=, that a note of yours hides it.
  Read under a note the user does not own, such as a teammate's mailbox
  drawn from its own root, it says which of its children the user has
  filed elsewhere or hidden in a fork. The marker follows any fraction,
  as in =1•C2/8=, and stands only on those two in-sides.
